## Vercel Web Analytics Implementation

Successfully installed and configured Vercel Web Analytics for this Next.js App Router project.

### Changes Made:

#### 1. Package Installation
- Installed `@vercel/analytics` package via npm
- Package version: latest available from npm registry

#### 2. Modified Files:

**app/layout.tsx**
- Added import statement: `import { Analytics } from '@vercel/analytics/next';`
- Added `<Analytics />` component to the root layout inside the `<body>` tag
- The Analytics component is now rendered on all pages of the application

**package.json & package-lock.json**
- Updated with @vercel/analytics dependency

### Implementation Details:

The implementation follows the official Vercel documentation (fetched from https://vercel.com/docs/analytics/quickstart) for Next.js App Router projects:
- Analytics component is placed in the root layout file
- Component is positioned at the end of the body tag as recommended
- No additional configuration is required
- The integration provides seamless route support for Next.js

### Testing Performed:

1. ✅ TypeScript type checking passed (`npm run typecheck`)
2. ✅ Production build completed successfully (`npm run build`)
3. ✅ All 25 routes compiled without errors
4. ✅ No type errors or build warnings introduced

### Verification:

After deployment to Vercel, analytics tracking can be verified by:
- Checking the Vercel dashboard for analytics data
- Inspecting browser's Network tab for Fetch/XHR requests to `/<unique-path>/view`

The Analytics component will automatically track page views and other user interactions once the application is deployed to Vercel's platform.
